From: airplay project
Subject: [PATCH] uxplay: handle CTRL_BREAK_EVENT in CtrlHandler so GUI hosts can stop cleanly

A parent that created the child with CREATE_NEW_PROCESS_GROUP (which disables CTRL_C for
the group) can only deliver CTRL_BREAK. Without this case CtrlHandler returns FALSE,
Windows kills the process and cleanup() (mDNS goodbye, GStreamer teardown) never runs.
---
--- a/uxplay.cpp
+++ b/uxplay.cpp
@@ -588,6 +588,7 @@
 static BOOL WINAPI CtrlHandler(DWORD signal) {
     switch (signal) {
     case CTRL_C_EVENT:
+    case CTRL_BREAK_EVENT:   /* GUI hosts send this to a CREATE_NEW_PROCESS_GROUP child; must run cleanup() */
     case CTRL_CLOSE_EVENT:
     case CTRL_SHUTDOWN_EVENT:
         if (gmainloop) {
